# UART Controlled LED Pattern Sequencer

## Overview

This project demonstrates a modular embedded firmware application developed for the VSDSquadron Mini development board based on the CH32V003 RISC-V microcontroller.

The application receives commands through UART and executes user-defined LED blink patterns on PD6. The firmware follows a layered architecture with separate GPIO and UART drivers, allowing easy reuse and maintenance.

The system accepts pattern commands from a serial terminal and converts them into LED ON/OFF sequences with fixed timing intervals.

---

## Target Hardware

- VSDSquadron Mini
- CH32V003 RISC-V Microcontroller
- Onboard/User LED connected to PD6
- UART1 Communication Interface

---

## Supported Drivers

- GPIO Driver
- UART Driver

---

## Features

- UART command interface
- LED pattern sequencing
- Runtime pattern execution
- STOP command support
- Modular driver architecture
- Register-level peripheral control

